---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/hero-about.png';
import { SOCIAL_LINKS } from '../consts';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Who Rob Henry is and what this site is for."
	pubDate={new Date('May 11 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		I'm Rob Henry — a southern boy who moved up north and became a web developer. I spent years in the 
		Microsoft ecosystem (.NET, ASP.NET MVC, Umbraco). The only problem with that is that it's not as 
		exciting as the rest of the technologies that are out there, unless you stay that small "hype circle". 
		I latched onto WordPress for a little while, because I wanted to learn it and possibly use that 
		knowledge for side gigs. But I dropped all that when I learned about Astro. I spent my <em>spare</em> 
		time learning it, but <strong>even</strong> that started to wane. <strong>Then</strong> I started 
		learning about Cloudflare and all the magic that it can do. <strong>Then</strong> Cloudflare acquired Astro. 
		<strong>Then</strong> I kept seeing the amazing things that people can build with AI.
	</p>
	<p>
		I finally decided that I'm going to create a new Astro site, host it on Cloudflare, and not worry about
		making content. I will add posts when I have something to say, but I'm not going to force it. I will
		work on the projects that I want to work on, and write about them if I find that there is something to say.
		That's what this site is for.
	</p>
	<p>
		As mentioned before, this site is for me, but I'm not greedy. If you find something useful here, I'd love 
		to hear it. Comments may come later; for now, find me on{' '}
		{
			SOCIAL_LINKS.map((link, index) => (
				<>
					{index > 0 && (index === SOCIAL_LINKS.length - 1 ? ' or ' : ', ')}
					<a href={link.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
						{link.name}
					</a>
				</>
			))
		}.
	</p>
</Layout>
